#---
# purpose: "byte_size/1 of a non-binary aborts with ArgumentError and Elixir's message"
# expect: abort
# oracle: self
# oracle.stamp: 9c03808e66e123e5
#---
# `byte_size/1`'s spec takes a bitstring, so a call whose argument is proven to
# be an atom is refused at compile time. The head of `[:x, "a"]` may be a
# binary, so the call compiles and the atom is refused when it runs.
defmodule Main do
  def main(), do: byte_size(hd([:x, "a"]))
end

Main.main()
